{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/866492-who-else-would-like-a-new-cambion-template","id":866492,"title":"Who else would like a new Cambion Template?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-16T12:37:39-07:00","id":866492,"title":"Who else would like a new Cambion Template?","content":"I think a new Cambion Template for playable Cambions would be cool.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what sort of powers in place of contracts or echoes that a Cambion should get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T13:40:25-07:00","id":867027,"title":"","content":"You mean a new cambion other than what we have in the playtest? I think there's enough there to build a player cambion. They'd be a mortal with the extra abilities thrown on.<br /> <br /> They have Wyrd, so they can see through the mask, travel the hedge, etc. Devour Glamour and Glamour Immunity give them a good foundation for being dangerous to fae things and Demonic Child makes them more durable than most. While it's not detailed, I'd let them spend Glamour on a 1:1 basis to clear a wound box unless it's from fire. If you don't want to be as generous, use vampires rules for healing. I wouldn't give them contracts or echos since the one in the rules makes no indication that they have them. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T00:27:37-07:00","id":867407,"title":"","content":"Erm, what cambion we have in playtest? I was aware of fae touched, but the cambions getting a 2 edition makeover is not something I was aware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T00:46:17-07:00","id":867422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/866492-who-else-would-like-a-new-cambion-template?p=867407#post867407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Erm, what cambion we have in playtest? I was aware of fae touched, but the cambions getting a 2 edition makeover is not something I was aware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look in the Dreamwalking preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T02:46:32-07:00","id":867453,"title":"","content":"Danke.<br /> <br /> Anyway, interesting, I was quite surprised at how predatory they made them, but then again I remember thinking the first edition version while interesting lacked oomph. <br /> <br /> Unholy terrors against glamour dependent foes, they aren't that dangerous to more mundane, or other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> For games in which going &quot;glamour nom nom nom&quot; wouldn't cut it, two ideas come to mind-<br /> <br /> 1) Since their concept is now glamour vampires, perhaps take inspiration from there and allow them to heal with glamour points and enhance their physical stats ala vampires,<br /> <br /> 2) If wanting to emphasize their psychic vampire schtick perhaps they can convert glamour into willpower points, making them larger than life dynamos as long as they feed but listless and sluggish without. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T16:23:33-07:00","id":867899,"title":"","content":"The 2e Cambion is too powerful to be a lesser template, they the NPC verion has 4 wyrd!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T18:22:23-07:00","id":868002,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but what's it being used for besides as a bonus to Devour Glamour rolls and (probably) how much Glamour they hold at any given time? It's not intended to be a minor template but I don't think it'd be OP if you houseruled them into a player option. It would be nice to learn more about them though, maybe get an expansion on their ability to be unholy horrors devouring hedge and hob alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T19:09:22-07:00","id":868044,"title":"","content":"I decided to take another look at the Wyrd and Glamour traits in the Playtest Doc to seem if I could tell what were the universal traits of being a Fae, most of which would apply to the Cambion.<br /> <br /> Under Glamour it seems clear that almost any Fae can Harvest Glamour from Mortal emotions if they can access the mortal world.<br /> <br /> So Incubi, Fae Touched, Hedge Beast Companions, Fetches, True Fae, Cambions, Changelings, but not Huntsmen (they don't use Glamour, which makes them oddly the most dangerous Fae to Cambions), nor Succubi (can't get off of the dreams), and nor Fae that never leave the Hedge or Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Hedge Bounty likewise is near universal for all Fae who can access it (leaving out Succubi who can't access it and Huntsmen who don't use Glamour).<br /> <br /> Dreams only for Changelings, Incubi, Succubi, Baku, and maybe Cambions in a very different way? (Devoure Glamour, eating the dream entirely instead of Harvesting it?).<br /> <br /> Wyrd. <br /> <br /> Basic Resistance Stat effect is universal. <br /> <br /> Boost to Longevity.<br /> <br /> Spend and Store more Glamour<br /> <br /> How Much Goblin Fruit the Cambion can carry into the Mortal World.<br /> <br /> How many Pledges a Cambion can have (Sealings appear to be universal for Fae except for Fetches).<br /> <br /> Seeing through the Mask.<br /> <br /> And that seems to be it that's applable to Cambions, although openning gateways to and from the hedge would make sense.<br /> <br /> Also a Playable Cambion might gain Clarity, instead of Intergity, which would grant the Cambion a potential Perception Bonus, Keening, and the ability to add Clarity to rolls to resist none Fae Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T19:21:42-07:00","id":868053,"title":"","content":"Side note, there is no reason their can't be animal Cambions as well as human Cambiobs, for regular animals are mortal too and some Onierans maybe be more compatible with animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T23:02:31-07:00","id":868211,"title":"","content":"Do animals dream in a way that connects to the hedge though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T05:00:45-07:00","id":868324,"title":"","content":"They don't have to, because Incubi can leave the hedge, mate with them, producing Animal Cambions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T12:53:05-07:00","id":873236,"title":"","content":"Yeah, shouldn't be too hard to make a PC cambion template. Maybe one who gains a soul, and thus an existence beyond the humanlike hob gets either Integrity or Clarity, as well as the ability to develop their powers from just filter feeding Glamour; their new sanity gives them focus and ambition.<br /> <br /> Really, the &quot;abominations&quot; aren't even that unplayable as is; they're just high-functioning sociopaths, and the thing about high-functioning is that they're usually perfectly good at being productive members of society, they're just bad with impulse control and instinctive empathy. For cambions, who need to emotionally manipulate people to survive? Lack of inherent remorse is probably a feature, not a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T15:31:04-07:00","id":873335,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what is supposed to be &quot;abominations&quot; about them anyways. <br /> <br /> I mean yeah, they eat Fae magic and don't need to eat, breath, drink, and can survive bleeding all over the place, but that makes them potentially dangerous, but also useful to the Fae.<br /> <br /> Also they're part Mortal, part human, born from a Mortal woman's womb or quickened by a human man's sperm, so there is no reason a Cambion can't have a soul, even if 50% is made up of dream stuff.<br /> <br /> There is no reason a Cambion has to be a villian, they're just a potential threat, but a Cambion at Wyrd 4, at most can hold 14 glamour at a time, so its not like a single Cambion could destroy the hedge, especially if the local changeling harvest enough Glamour as an offering to keep it fed.<br /> <br /> And as a half human, its not really a hob, sure it can survive in the hedge better then almost anything, but its basic habitat appears to be the mortal world.<br /> <br /> The Cambion is part Fae and part mortal like the Changeling and the Fae Touched.<br /> <br /> Still I do a agree playing a Cambion should be easy enough, it just need to be flushed out enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}